{ A knight fork attacks two targets. When one target is the king, the opponent must answer the check, often leaving no time to save the other target. } 1. Ne7+ Kf8 2. Nxc8 { Illustrative line. Ne7+ makes a double attack with check. Black must move the king; ...Kf8 is one legal reply. The knight then takes the rook with Nxc8. Check the landing square before celebrating the pattern. A fork fails if the forking piece can be captured, if the second target moves with check, or if the first target can answer while saving the second. Here the king cannot capture the knight, and the rook cannot remove the check. } *

