{ Exercise. Try the questions in the book before reading this line. } 1. Nd7+ Kg8 2. Nxb8 { Illustrative line. Nd7+ attacks f8 and b8 from d7. The board has shifted, so use the knight's actual L-shaped moves rather than remembering e7 from Model A. After ...Kg8, Nxb8 captures the rook. Other legal king moves still leave the rook forked. Check that no black pawn attacks the knight's landing square d7. The king is in check. A rook move that does not capture the knight or otherwise remove the knight check is illegal. The checking component supplies the time needed to collect the second target. } *

