{ An absolute pin forbids moves that expose your king to check. It does not freeze a piece by a special rule; normal king-safety rules determine exactly which moves remain legal. } 1... Kf7 { Illustrative line. Black cannot move the knight while the king stays on e8 and the pin remains. A knight cannot slide along the pin line, so all of its jumps would uncover a rook check on its own king. ...Kf7 is a legal way to step out of the pin. This is a rule demonstration, not a claim that Black can save the ending against best play. Once the king is off the e-file, moving the knight no longer exposes that particular check. } *

